.TH tkukeynav n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkukeynav
.PP
Keyboard focus navigation helpers: consistent Tab / Shift\-Tab traversal plus Return\-to\-next\-field form ergonomics, the way data\-entry users expect. Pure Tk, works with classic and ttk inputs. Bindings are per widget and released on \fB<Destroy>\fR.
.SS Movement
.CS
::tkutils::tkukeynav::next $w      ;# focus next widget in tab order (returns it)
::tkutils::tkukeynav::prev $w      ;# focus previous
.CE
.SS "Per\-widget bindings"
.CS
::tkutils::tkukeynav::enable $w ?-onreturn cmd? ?-onescape cmd? ?-tab 0|1?
::tkutils::tkukeynav::disable $w
.CE
.PP
\fB\-tab\fR (default 1) installs Tab/Shift\-Tab traversal that also works inside widgets which would otherwise swallow Tab. \fB\-onreturn\fR/\fB\-onescape\fR run on Return/Escape and stop further handling.
.SS "Form ergonomics"
.CS
::tkutils::tkukeynav::form $container ?-onsubmit cmd? ?-wrap 0|1? ?-onescape cmd?
.CE
.PP
Treats the focusable input descendants of \fB$container\fR (entries, combos, spinboxes, text, listboxes, check/radio) as a form: Return advances to the next field; on the last field it runs \fB\-onsubmit\fR (or wraps to the first when \fB\-wrap 1\fR). Returns the ordered list of fields.
.CS
package require tkutils::tkukeynav
ttk::frame .form
foreach n {name email phone} { pack [ttk::entry .form.$n] }
pack .form
tkukeynav::form .form -onsubmit {saveContact}
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Errors carry \fB{TKUTILS TKUKEYNAV <REASON>}\fR (\fBNOWIDGET\fR, \fBOPTION\fR).
.SS Demo
.CS
tclsh examples/demo-tkukeynav.tcl
.CE
